checks.numbers:
C remote helper on board A (ttyACM0), retry on; kill -TERM of the parent pid, sampled at 20 Hz:
- websocket run 1: parent, capture child and flock all gone at +0.01 s;
- --tcp: all three gone at +0.041 s;
- websocket run 2: all three gone at +0.045 s.
In each run /proc/locks lost the child's FLOCK on inode 00:06:715 (ttyACM0). An open with flock afterwards succeeded ('OPENED and flocked'), which also shows the exclusive mode (TIOCEXCL) was released. Parent exit status 143. The child's SigCgt was 0000000100004001 (SIGTERM caught).

Four sources for 60 s: esp32c5-ttyACM0 and esp32c5-ttyACM1 (Wi-Fi), esp32c5zigbee-ttyACM2, esp32c5btle-ttyACM3. Prior radios as in hw2's n1c: A in BLE, B, C and D in Wi-Fi.
C local: all 4 running with 0 error samples. Packets 709/1295/0/1066. Devices: 47 Wi-Fi, 13 BTLE. Launched -> capturing:
- BLE->Wi-Fi 1.58 s (n1c: 1.62);
- Wi-Fi->Wi-Fi 0.98 s;
- Wi-Fi->zigbee 1.48 s (hw2: 1.49-1.50);
- Wi-Fi->BTLE 2.50 s, with a USB re-enumeration (n1c: 2.50).
Python, one process: all 4 running, 0 errors. Packets 750/1025/0/1062. Devices: 48 Wi-Fi, 17 BTLE. Helper start -> capturing: 1.29/1.50/1.75/3.32 s.
C remote, 4 processes, first run: the three non-BTLE sources were fine (1616/1146/0 packets; capturing at 1.14/1.17/1.45 s). The BTLE source got 0 packets and 150 error samples: board D re-enumerated on the Wi-Fi->BLE switch, then gave 'no answer, reconnecting' and a 15 s give-up 3 times. The board answered no START until an esptool reset, after which it came up in BLE mode.
Two repeats of the C remote run: all 4 running, 0 errors.
- repeat 2: 1336/1310/0/1027 packets; capturing at 1.00/1.28/1.40/2.58 s;
- repeat 3: 1282/1182/0/1090 packets; capturing at 1.01/1.28/1.41/2.50 s.
For comparison, hw2 n1c had 1688/1700/0/1822 packets and g4 had 3455/3082/0/3105 in 120 s. The difference is ambient traffic.

